-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ming-treasure-voyages.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ming treasure voyages</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ming treasure voyages were seven large maritime expeditions led by the admiral Zheng He between 1405 and 1433.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ming-yuzhen"><span class="enc-name">Ming Yuzhen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ming Yuzhen was a commander of Xu Shouhui's Red Turban regime who led an army up the Yangtze and took Chongqing in 1357.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mingun-pahtodawgyi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mingun-pahtodawgyi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mingun Pahtodawgyi</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mingun Pahtodawgyi is a huge unfinished brick stupa at Mingun, on the west bank of the Irrawaddy north of Mandalay, begun by King Bodawpaya in 1790.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mingyi-nyo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mingyi-nyo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mingyi Nyo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mingyi Nyo was the founder of the Toungoo dynasty of Burma, ruler of the small principality of Toungoo on the Sittaung river from 1485.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mingyi-swa"><span class="enc-name">Mingyi Swa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mingyi Swa was crown prince of Toungoo Burma, son of King Nanda Bayin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/minh-huong"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/minh-huong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name